{"generatedAt":1795232545733,"status":[{"name":"Awaiting build approval","count":1,"rows":[{"id":"ALBUM-3","title":"Choose the tech stack and scaffold the app","risk":"Medium (app scaffold, edits project.md).","next":"awaiting-build since 2026-11-20 11:57 pm UTC: spec 111a741","stage":"awaiting-build","stageAt":"2026-11-20T23:57:11Z","owner":"dbeallor","issueUrl":"https://github.com/dbeallor/album-ranker/issues/3","threadLink":"<t3-thread://v2/fa8d9b7c-8629-46cf-bc5f-096683c72719/thread:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3A1a6947f3-c322-4d5e-88c8-a05ef2b5e692%3Adelegate-task%3A1504ee0a-8415-4ad4-b57e-e084f4111c28>","specUrl":"https://github.com/dbeallor/album-ranker/blob/111a7416151ea44bb58bb3dc3eefa188e432906f/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-20-album-3-stack-scaffold.md","detail":{"kind":"spec","sections":[{"name":"Goal","text":"Pick the stack for the album ranker and commit a runnable, empty scaffold, so tickets #4 to #10 have a place to build and real Test, Lint and Typecheck commands to run.\n\nThe shape is fixed by the MVP spec: one web app with a small server, one SQLite file, run on localhost, config from environment variables."},{"name":"Out of scope","text":"- Any album, ranking or rating feature.\n- Database tables, a SQLite driver or an ORM (#4).\n- CI, deployment and a password gate.\n- Styling beyond the framework defaults. No CSS framework is added."},{"name":"Calls I made","text":"Surprising first.\n\n- **Next.js** over SvelteKit or Remix, for ecosystem size and drag and drop libraries. It is the heaviest of the three.\n- **This PR edits `docs/agents/project.md`** (Commands, Areas, one new repo invariant). The ticket asks for the first two; that file is on the approval path, so this spec should not be auto-approved.\n- **New repo invariant**: never commit `data/` or a SQLite file, since the database will hold the user's rankings.\n- **`DATABASE_PATH` added now** with a default, though nothing opens a database until #4, so `.env.example` and the config patter